        'rawContent': '{{Vehicle Information|\n|name = XV-1 (Imperial Experimental Chassis)\n|image = \n|caption = XV-1 (Imperial Experimental Chassis)\n|mission_profile = Experimental Drop-Capable Tank Chassis\n|crew = 2 (Commander, driver)\n|manufacturer = [[Royal Imperial Labs]]\n|operator = [[Royal Imperial Army]]\n|powerplant = 1 x [[Royal Imperial Labs]] 2mW Fuel Cell\n|propulsion = 2 x [[Royal Imperial Labs]] Electric-Powered Turbine Engine\n|max_speed = \n|fixed_weapons = 1 x Dummy Test Cannon (inoperable, for weight trials only)\n|armor = [[Royal Imperial Labs]] Series-1 Composite Armor\n|shields = \n}}\n\n*Designation: Experimental Drop-Capable Tank Chassis\r\n*Length: 8 meters\r\n*Width: 3.5 meters\r\n*Height: 2.4 meters\r\n*Power: 1 x [[Royal Imperial Labs]] 2mW Fuel Cell\r\n*Propulsion: 2 x [[Royal Imperial Labs]] Electric-Powered Turbine Engine\r\n*Suspension: Torsion Bar\r\n**On-Road Speed: 70KPH\r\n**Off-Road Speed: 50KPH\r\n**Range: 850KM\r\n*Crew: 2 (Commander, driver)\r\n*Communications System: [[Royal Imperial Labs]] Series-1 Radio Transceiver\r\n*Sensors: None\r\n*Processing System: None\r\n*Armament: \r\n**1 x Dummy Test Cannon (inoperable, for weight trials only)\r\n*Defenses: \r\n**[[Royal Imperial Labs]] Series-1 Composite Armor\r\n*Operators:\r\n**[[Royal Imperial Army]]\r\n*Number built: 5\r\n*Unit cost: 75,000 [[Imperial Credits]]\r\n*Manufacturers:\r\n**[[Royal Imperial Labs]]\r\n\r\nThe XV-1 was the first Imperial drop-capable combat vehicle. It was a proof-of-concept vehicle, using a fuel-cell electric engine and a standardized dropship hookup which could be matched to any of the dropships employed by the Royal Imperial Navy and Air Force. It was never armed or deployed to the field. Lessons learned and design decisions made were eventually used in the design of "[[:Category:Imperial Military Specification|Military Specification 3]]", the [[M-3 Enforcer]]\r\n\r\n[[Category:Vehicles]]'
